.page strings 1 print the printable strings in a file

# SYNOPSIS
*strings* [*-n* _MIN_] [*-a*] [_FILE_]

# DESCRIPTION
`strings` scans _FILE_ (or standard input) and prints every run of printable ASCII characters (tabs included) that is at least four characters long, one per line. It is the quick way to find the readable parts of a binary.

# OPTIONS
@ *-n* _MIN_
    Print runs of at least _MIN_ characters instead of four.
@ *-a*
    Accepted for compatibility; the whole file is always scanned.

# EXAMPLES
    strings /bin/hello | head
    strings -n 8 /bin/gapsh | grep -i gap

# SEE ALSO
hexdump(1), grep(1), od(1)
